  "findings": [
    "Two new Android 1.0.46/build53 production-tagged read failures belong to the same anonymous device and PDF content session.",
    "First failure followed 115 cumulative playback seconds. Next resume failed after 19ms without first audio. Third resume produced first audio in 2300ms and accumulated 1894 playback seconds before content_closed.",
    "The reviewed 3fe41d62 source routes generation_failed through the generic exception exit in PlaybackController; CancellationException is rethrown first and obsolete playback work is ignored.",
    "A partial cached prefix can be synchronously enqueued before a new HTTP request. This is a possible local fast-failure path, not proof of the incident cause.",
    "No underlying client exception or client-to-server request key was retained. Seven Direct disconnects exactly match proxy cancellations but are not linked to either 19:05 client failure.",
    "Previous Global, Direct, US proxy and R134 releases remain deployed. This observation and source audit contain no new fix or deployment for these two failures."
  ],
